WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:05.340
With so many big, world-shaking things happening
in every episode of Game of Thrones, it can

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:08.050
be easy to overlook some of the smaller moments.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:11.889
Here's a spoiler-filled look at some things
only real fans noticed in the final season

00:00:11.889 --> 00:00:12.820
of Game of Thrones.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:16.960
Since the beginning of the show, Daenerys
has adopted different traditions and styles

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:20.700
from the various tribes and groups she's led
and joined, and perhaps the most influential

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.640
group in her young life is the Dothraki, thanks
to the fact that she became a queen of the

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.050
warrior tribe upon her marriage to Khal Drogo.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:31.130
The Dothraki place an enormous importance
upon the length and style of their hair, especially

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:35.210
for the men: the more braids a man sports,
the more victories he's won in battle, and

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:39.460
a Dothraki warrior only cuts his hair if he
loses a fight, so the longer the mane, the

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:40.659
more formidable the warrior.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:45.320
"When Dothraki are defeated in combat, they
cut off their braid so the whole world can

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:46.140
see their shame.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:49.400
Khal Drogo has never been defeated."

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.900
As a result, Daenerys has sported a lengthy
mane featuring a fierce tangle of braids for

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:54.660
several seasons.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:58.839
But the fifth episode of the eighth season
finds her at a disadvantage, having lost two

00:00:58.839 --> 00:01:04.190
of her most trusted advisors, Jorah and Missandei
. When Tyrion checks on her at Dragonstone,

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:08.110
her braids are mussed, undone, and ragged,
letting the audience know that the Dragon

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:11.700
Queen is losing her grip, and will end up
risking everything to get back on top.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:16.660
When Daenerys was married to the warrior lord
Khal Drogo in Thrones' first season, she didn't

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:20.190
anticipate having to fight all of her own
battles, mostly because Drogo, a prideful

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:23.280
and formidable fighter, was all too happy
to wage war on her behalf.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:27.690
When Daenerys told him she was pregnant with
his son, who was prophesied to be a Messiah-like

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:31.140
figure known as the "Stallion Who Would Mount
the World," Drogo made a passionate promise

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:33.400
to take the Iron Throne on Daenerys' behalf.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:45.860
That sort of violent destruction is exactly
what Daenerys and her Dothraki hordes unleashed

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:48.120
on King's Landing in the fifth episode of
the final season.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:52.390
It seemed out of character, until you remember
that Daenerys made a similar pact with the

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:54.080
Dothraki back in season six.

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:04.380
Looks like she has more than kept both of
those promises.

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:09.220
After losing her husband, Daenerys made several
attempts to find armies and benefactors to

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:13.660
back her in the war to come, and during Thrones'
second season, she ran afoul of the warlocks

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:17.110
of Qarth, who stole her dragons and lured
her into the terrifying and mystical House

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:18.380
of the Undying to get them back.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.520
Naturally, Daenerys charged into the temple
to track down her "children" and experienced

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:26.420
a number of visions along the way, seeing
everything from her late husband Drogo and

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:29.220
their lost child to a battered and seemingly
destroyed Iron Throne.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:34.460
Standing in an empty and ravaged Throne Room,
it seems as if Daenerys is surrounded by snow,

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:37.560
but thanks to the aftermath of King's Landing
in the wake of her ruthless and murderous

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:41.900
siege, it's clear that her vision has come
true, and it's not snow, but ashes.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:45.700
Many viewers always believed that the snow
was a sign of the Night King, but perhaps,

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:49.680
at this point, Daenerys' reign of fire and
blood is even more dangerous and destructive

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:53.840
than the Night King himself, and before long,
audiences will likely see Daenerys standing

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:57.500
in the real, ransacked version of the Throne
Room, ready and determined to take whatever

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:59.000
is left of the Iron Throne itself.

